###1) Completing the square

The number that will help us complete the square is $\left(\dfrac{\blueD{18}}{2}\right)^2=\goldD{81}$:

$\begin{align}
x^2+\blueD{18}x&=8
\\\\
x^2+\blueD{18}x+\goldD{81}&=89&&\text{Add 81.}
\\\\
(x+9)^2&=89&&\text{Factor.}
\end{align}$

[[☃ explanation 1]]

###2) Solving the equation

$\begin{align}
(x+9)^2&=89
\\\\
\sqrt{(x+9)^2}&=\pm\sqrt{89}&&\text{Take the square root.}
\\\\
x+9&= \pm \sqrt{89}
\\\\
x&= -9 \pm \sqrt{89}&&\text{Subtract }9.
\end{align}$
